southwest medical wants to remind the  community about the importance of infant  immunization so i spoke with one of  their doctors  to learn more check it out so coming up  later this month it's infant  immunization  week and we're talking about the  importance of infant  immunization so let's start with that  what do you what are your thoughts  yes so immunizations is one of the most  important ways that we can protect  children  from preventable childhood diseases and  even though we may not realize it  a lot of things that we take for granted  now a lot of diseases that used to be  pretty rampant here in the united states  and around the world  have been minimized because of  immunizations  and because of that i think parents  don't understand the  significance of immunizations because we  don't see these diseases as much anymore  but we've learned that when immunization  rates go down  these diseases can pop back up which is  really important to emphasize again why  it's important to immunize your child  on time and regularly according to the  schedule recommended by the american  academy of pediatrics and the cdc  which vaccinations do you think children  actually need  so this really depends on the age of the  child right now we are  basically protecting kids from more than  14 of  preventable diseases through  immunizations so it's important to know  based on your child's age and their  current immunization status  to talk with their doctor to find out  what they need  whether it is for their child early  childhood immunizations  or for what they need to go to school  and day care and this is very important  that they are up to date especially if  they're going to be in a setting with  other kids the whole reason they're  given these  immunizations at this early age is that  younger children are more vulnerable  to these childhood infections so if  you're waiting until your child gets  older  the risk of them actually acquiring the  disease is when they're younger  and these vaccines have been tested over  the years for safety  and it's really important to note that  you are really preventing some very  serious complications  not just children but preteens  teens and adults should also see what  their immunization status is  now we know adults have the opportunity  to get the coveted vaccine which is  highly recommended for everyone who's  able to get it which is wonderful  soon they'll be releasing data on  coveted vaccinations for  teenagers too and we're eagerly waiting  to see  what the ctc says about that but it is  important to get updated on those shots  and certain immunizations such as for  pertussis or whooping cough  the teenagers do need to get their  booster dose to continue that protection  and adults do too so it's not something  that just stops  at childhood it continues on throughout  your years and  into adulthood southwest medical has  locations across  southern nevada just call  or 702-877-5199 smalv.com for more
 

